<title>JAPAN: Isuzu falls on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Isuzu falls on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Isuzu Motors Ltd shares fell on profit-taking on Friday morning after the shares were boosted on Thursday by news that Isuzu and General Motors Corp of the United States were considering transferring GM's diesel engine development and production to Isuzu.</p>
<p>As of 0149 GMT, the shares were down 10 yen at 425 on turnover of 3.7 million shares, making it the third-most heavily traded issue on the first section of the Tokyo bourse.  </p>
<p>&quot;Some market participants think there are no big reasons to keep buying car maker shares as there is speculation that growth in demand is likely to slow soon,&quot; a trader at a second-tier brokerage said.</p>
<p>&quot;Even if there is good news about cars, it only feeds the market for a day,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
